## If the person gets stuck

**"I don't know which category."** Walk through their work. Match on the outcome they drove, not the tool they used. If they led change across a team, surface AI Transformation Leader.

**"I don't have hard metrics."** Ask: who noticed this work? What did they say? What changed in someone's calendar, budget, or headcount? "My manager stopped asking for the weekly report because it auto-generates" is a metric.

**"My work isn't good enough."** Most people undersell. Ask what the old way looked like and how many people were doing it that way. The gap between old and new is usually bigger than they think.

**"I'm nominating someone else."** Use the same rubric. Interview them about the other person's work. Focus on what they've directly observed, not guesses.

**"Should I do the video?"** Yes. Video submissions score higher because judges hear the thinking behind the work. Five prompts, five minutes. Record at [videoask.com/fcczkudp7](https://www.videoask.com/fcczkudp7).

